Rule (plan Milestone 2, restated by the Orchestrator; applied to the v2 rows 69, 71, 72, 73, 74, 75):
  among the v2 configurations, the highest hit@5 such that, compared with the v2 BASELINE (69): no ticker's hit@5 decreases; no FIGURE question in the top 5
  under 69 leaves the top 5. Ties: MRR, then the smaller change from the current defaults (sum of absolute weight differences). 69 always qualifies.
  Protected FIGURE questions (22 of 28 in the top 5 under 69): aapl-01 aapl-02 aapl-06 aapl-07 aapl-11 aapl-12 aapl-13 aapl-14 msft-02 msft-04 msft-10 msft-11
  msft-12 msft-13 msft-14 nvda-01 nvda-03 nvda-08 nvda-11 nvda-12 nvda-13 nvda-14
  69 (kw 0.5 fig 1.0) QUALIFIES (baseline)
  71 (kw 0.5 fig 0.0) out: MSFT 0.714286 < 0.785714; NVDA 0.571429 < 0.642857; msft-13 1 -> not in window; nvda-12 5 -> not in window
  72 (kw 0.5 fig 0.5) out: NVDA 0.571429 < 0.642857; nvda-12 5 -> not in window
  73 (kw 0.5 fig 2.0) QUALIFIES: hit@5 0.785714, MRR 0.644473, change 1.0
  74 (kw 1.0 fig 1.0) out: msft-04 4 -> 8 (MSFT stays 0.785714 because msft-07 7 -> 4)
  75 (kw 0.5 fig 1.5) QUALIFIES: hit@5 0.785714, MRR 0.644473, change 0.5
  Order: 69 (0.785714, 0.655187, 0.0) > 75 (0.785714, 0.644473, 0.5) > 73 (0.785714, 0.644473, 1.0)
  => Winner id 69, the current defaults: rrf-k 60, rrf-vector-weight 1.0, rrf-keyword-weight 0.5, rrf-figure-weight 1.0. No weight default changes.
  The figure weight survived measurement: turning the leg off (71) costs hit@5 0.785714 -> 0.738095, hit@1 0.547619 -> 0.380952, MRR 0.655187 -> 0.533362.

Floor: 0.785714 - 0.1 = 0.685714, rounded down to a multiple of 0.05 = 0.65. rag.evaluation.min-hit-at-5 0.50 -> 0.65 (application.yaml, RetrievalEvaluationProperties
  default and javadoc); the v1-derived 0.50 is superseded because the set changed (the value happens to rise, so nothing is lowered).
  Tests: RetrievalEvaluationSetTests.theBoundHitAt5FloorIsTheSetV2Derivation (bound yaml value) and RetrievalEvaluationSetLoaderTests (class default) assert 0.65.

